{"title":"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2(Another_Pair_of_Similar_Triangles)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2(Another Pair of Similar Triangles)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(a_bit_long)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (a bit long)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Short_with_Trig)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Short with Trig)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> with a right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lies in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd04dad7bcbb82e2fb88a632026bca2bb74a61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=CD,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784c6bf43ef7181384b52b412b4636c710ecbedd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=EB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> and the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58c70d044c65766c81e58a798288ece9b7a02c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC:DE=4:3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"130\" height=\"13\" />. What is the ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/7/1f7b944321f888d7fb5355e4c6ba0af8c22ebc3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD:DB?$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/8/618f85c360aff21cd251b8016e035b5f8446f7ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }2:3\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }2:\\sqrt{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }1:1\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }3:\\sqrt{5}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }3:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"504\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ae177bee89e4c1255d4e88a7934a44ee797c07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = CD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df637c7e5d21045f84cb4a1b48b84e35ee192c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = EB = 3$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f369266e464a676c25b9b02f73b874edb27e9ffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = \\alpha$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/2/442eca2e1a78ef29fe406750a91560e2a8f0b435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\beta = 90^{\\circ} - \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c45c55274427f284efb69f46e4c5917a5ae7f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> are isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d432bcab13b0aac869092e0b341e8ddeb4186994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC = \\alpha$\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/a/dfae8079a8d7f39bed761e08c17253e357fca530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDE = \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4183a8199a3fe0113fac1eb25d0ff8674fbef172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDE = 180^{\\circ} - \\alpha - \\beta = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"232\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b984c55719cc5f992ee62656d920ac15c78d9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1a2cb4ff1720f169ddde1726c1a5a1ab816ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-4-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" /> triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf7200c227276a7507b17341f46fc3d5a0bbd16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = 5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/94432b32b7de2903b65d75f243d7124e5cfd39eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB = 5+3 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/45755a53eaf9419774614cdba9dfbe8927b27bca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2-\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> triangle.\n</p><p>In isosceles triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/7/0f7a55113a84ee4c04eb66f66d08310c32533ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c45c55274427f284efb69f46e4c5917a5ae7f3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, drop altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />; denote the feet of these altitudes by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e17d85b5f5e7a48245e2662246a88ed0d253b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711d39585594f410327fda0915f4ce6cad872b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> respectively. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995c16d9e5de5fe1980e6007ec30ea48c8dc454d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACP_C \\sim \\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" /> by AAA similarity, so we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8bdd710a34edf2e21a165707b0fd884ddba1421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP_C = P_CD = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"153\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/5/7155e079877da0f16f9a654f95072e83b2846cf2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 2 \\times \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"111\" height=\"41\" />. Similarly, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/2/a221b8b5ac16eca9593ba83ded71edd2ca812644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 2 \\times \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"116\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d32cdc358307802be0bfbf2a3cf9cbdba92e3a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD:DB = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"179\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2.28Another_Pair_of_Similar_Triangles.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2(Another_Pair_of_Similar_Triangles)\">Solution 2(Another Pair of Similar Triangles)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2(Another Pair of Similar Triangles)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ae177bee89e4c1255d4e88a7934a44ee797c07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = CD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df637c7e5d21045f84cb4a1b48b84e35ee192c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = EB = 3$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" />. By the Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf7200c227276a7507b17341f46fc3d5a0bbd16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = 5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48af5ed6fb337504fecbb39131c378f6aa360a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e2f5d6ff93ebace9e84a0679ce1cf9d21328cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 4\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Next, drop <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> perpendicularly and call the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. We notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/3/ab3398b2986366888512d70313c10375d4a52823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EBP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are similar to each other by AAA similarity, and we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41a79e91d3cbe0c45f680041bbb657f3bcf1affb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{EB}{AB} = \\frac{3}{4\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{PB}{CB} \\implies PB = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}} \\implies BD = \\frac{12}{\\sqrt{5}} \\implies AD = \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}}\\]\" width=\"542\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Simplifying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c86d84519be482a88836566142be7d761784ea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD:AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f8e03288d6daf954de9a983df33b538ac62f58a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD:AD = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User%EF%BC%9AIcosahedron0288#Created_Pages\" title=\"User：Icosahedron0288\">Icosahedron0288</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/8/6481d8c7286cae111d77b62c95d3c9863eb8b50d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=CD=4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"125\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d1573aae5cc87bf54a9a25bcf848a261fbcf10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=EB=3x$\" width=\"126\" height=\"12\" />. (For this solution, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is to the right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />). Also let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b8919729d9fdfe021f1649a9eb1a40baa6ffad07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A = t^{\\circ}$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/585789f9a8291ebaeeb7697e5e279aac86675a42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACD = \\left(180-2t\\right)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a8740afe3ffe62d4b5a89fbf1e88c5dd2ef6ea3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DCB = \\left(2t - 90\\right)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"19\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2c5ba9c78f49c3730b7a7dc97237ec5ed534e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B = \\left(90-t\\right)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" />, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087720e86fc05ee70599980886cf9e3f5c454779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BED = 2t^{\\circ}$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />. This further implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/5260e19c04988a7ef3f3805cb76b762293f14a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEC = \\left(180 - 2t\\right)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"19\" />. \n</p><p>Now we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/9563fa4d6cf22371144b97006c967292a04b5529.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDE = 180^{\\circ} - \\angle ECD - \\angle DEC = 180^{\\circ} - 2t^{\\circ} + 90^{\\circ} - 180^{\\circ} + 2t^{\\circ} = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"578\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b984c55719cc5f992ee62656d920ac15c78d9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> is a right triangle, with side lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e634348f8df9eaeac4ced35db64d08a906532e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87e9f9eb8f39820b3b8cd2c4b06e10d90e0d3b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> (by the Pythagorean Theorem, or simply the Pythagorean triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1a2cb4ff1720f169ddde1726c1a5a1ab816ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3-4-5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />). Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab7625157b4820fa276a4bc4e6c7981f5c06e312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> (by definition), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5d7dfc7b44fa3b9dc4e66daba4023a9ef019dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=5x+3x = 8x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"157\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc90ca77fea2abdc02123687dcc4e020ef7bcf4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=4\\sqrt{5}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/343b9c3d65bbd9726f65a0358b4ae68865a836f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\left(2t^{\\circ}\\right)} = 2 \\cos^{2}{t^{\\circ}} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"19\" /> (by the double angle formula), giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e1635f2fdc2ff296098aac282221537ba63b2d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right)^2 - 1 = -\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"155\" height=\"46\" />.\n</p><p>By the Law of Cosines in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f007680c47a068a3aef3f4c57e9484da78281a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BED$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9d2c7dd2dfed34fd7540b7a28f7f4735824fccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = d$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ebbf71bcd07aabf481f5815f049be6dbdb6a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split}&amp;d^2 = (3x)^2+(3x)^2-2\\cdot\\frac{-3}{5}(3x)(3x) \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\ &amp;d^2 = 18x^2 + \\frac{54x^2}{5} = \\frac{144x^2}{5} \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\ &amp;d = \\frac{12x}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{split}\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"130\" /> Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c3f6418894e78bc008dba563ed425d563350522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = AB - BD = 4x\\sqrt{5} - \\frac{12x}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{8x}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"308\" height=\"42\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8dd4a11881a128607df5e844f2a97d898130b456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\left(\\frac{8x}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{12x}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right)} = \\frac{8}{12} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -30px\" width=\"201\" height=\"69\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_2\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>WLOG, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/4815797dac93e88d573872883cf189cb1b345711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=CD=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59f2b2844a277868ff62df840e00801b29f16c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=EB=3$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d30a587c22234a1e11eeaca03ed110e7de4cad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDE = 180^{\\circ} - \\angle ADC - \\angle BDE = 180^{\\circ} - \\angle DAC - \\angle DBE = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"544\" height=\"16\" />. Because of this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a 3-4-5 right triangle. Draw the altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929635b933267579ee98277d9ee450978e3ff875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85f448517195cbdc424948dcb01df3282f099092.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> by the base-height triangle area formula. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/6816e3f70d91b2115986ef939cbed51ad6b813b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> (AA).  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44bb493d6663354613438a96e312f7c8fcae3611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DF}{AC} = \\frac{BD}{AB} = \\frac35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"128\" height=\"37\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/3/a734cf9a56f3bcb7607275bbc8dd7451d3d634ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d655213558d61b1f944b62d4485ccf86d2073f37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD:DB$\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69c84a65ba2fe6274bbeb39f53f53d7f5120d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"80\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Thegreatboy90\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28a_bit_long.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(a_bit_long)\">Solution 4 (a bit long)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (a bit long)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>WLOG, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ae177bee89e4c1255d4e88a7934a44ee797c07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = CD = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0df637c7e5d21045f84cb4a1b48b84e35ee192c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = EB = 3$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" />. Notice that in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e5170b3a48d96da708932026f0e94194f415b0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/48287337f8d90c7aa46ebddd16ae8088f1d6d773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle BAC + m\\angle ABC = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42f271b8221d56650f45152cebb49a8368b052c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = CD$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e016704b1a81aab0c542aa53c778e90f62eb762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE = EB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6019f7147369b0cc761b0476293b9208582193.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle DAC = m\\angle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"171\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd5185221c08e254232ce5070db921400f0d812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle DBE = m\\angle BDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"173\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/518e3972079df174af644642048491614486bbc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle ADC + m\\angle BDE = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52f411a4b2b4264a2ca139f595247150a3bfb597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EDC$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is right. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebf7200c227276a7507b17341f46fc3d5a0bbd16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = 5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> by 3-4-5 triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48af5ed6fb337504fecbb39131c378f6aa360a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/e/69e2f5d6ff93ebace9e84a0679ce1cf9d21328cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 4\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />. Define point F such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is an altitude; we know the area of the whole triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and we know the hypotenuse is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1d8d49bd04ec238c372f249f77d023673c48431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbccd9877d5af2afe550c4253d3988bd0edb3ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF = \\frac{16}{4\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot2=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"167\" height=\"43\" />. By the geometric mean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/9/629ecf7ffae1fea764c4131d6254456b6a237f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\left(4\\sqrt{5}-x\\right)=4\\sqrt{5}x-x^{2}=\\left(\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{64}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"343\" height=\"48\" />. Solving the quadratic we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/4/d54f712a96262a79e32cfc3627c49b9ea0c6a346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{10\\sqrt{5}\\pm6\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/5/37521a5ebd1c92953a549a9fbf193d588ae864e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5} or \\frac{16\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" />. For now, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/9769375c6ffd871accab68b768a995fd1efb33a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"43\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c1fd29f42cac4435e72367600f7d7b3fbb6219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FB=4\\sqrt{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}=\\frac{16\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"219\" height=\"43\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> splits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> into two parts (quick congruence by Leg-Angle) so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da26aa958045b532a2d6f7216d0759e76091e47d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = AF = \\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"145\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f010905105f490cdbd29e29735d8b309fe4ce72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB = FB - FD = \\frac{16\\sqrt{5}}{5}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}=\\frac{12\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"338\" height=\"43\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae37162fed12d0ad42798b67b9b11aec2b7c074.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 2\\cdot\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{5}=\\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"176\" height=\"43\" />. Now we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/823c98c373f66f9a5935fd7c512c4551be7f0a36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AD}{DB}=\\frac{\\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{5}}{\\frac{12\\sqrt{5}}{5}}=\\frac{8\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\cdot\\frac{5}{12\\sqrt{5}}=\\frac{8}{12}=\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"304\" height=\"55\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69c84a65ba2fe6274bbeb39f53f53d7f5120d67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"80\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Short_with_Trig.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Short_with_Trig)\">Solution 5 (Short with Trig)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Short with Trig)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc0b95fe13bd5123c01c6761096fc522863b99d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B=\\theta_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/863349af57a4178b30675642cb51a0d600127204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A=90-\\theta_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/a/eca378432bddfcd3ead19364099ac976c30bfccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=AD$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/672cac8fef2978eaf3eb78e247d44470047d7898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADC=90-\\theta_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"17\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb94f5afd54e5eb6892abaf7a140db0040316e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDE=\\theta_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8ebd15cdcc848718da8139a8e3106fec3bc0081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EDC=180-\\theta_1-(90-\\theta_1)=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"284\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b9e3b4859c5a49ea66f0add510fa64a7f02bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup CDE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is right. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/4815797dac93e88d573872883cf189cb1b345711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=CD=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59f2b2844a277868ff62df840e00801b29f16c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=EB=3$\" width=\"116\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa1b20141d9f1abe495a7a2ba5db938d375c86c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/73483cbff11524553c6c51303c22835d3780db66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DEC=\\angle ACD=\\theta_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"17\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49a9c380fde88d8b13431bea49744fa273ec68e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta_2=\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"83\" height=\"38\" /> so we can apply the Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e465587d1b453f12a05efd5b8c3626803be6302c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup ACD$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b9815936c348fa6486b97f60a64bb8c4c074ee52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=\\sqrt{32-32\\cdot{\\frac{3}{5}}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot{32}} \\Longrightarrow \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"312\" height=\"48\" />. Doing Pythagorean for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66492998689e8303534c9e4f3ba1fa650fd41f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/d/d1d8d49bd04ec238c372f249f77d023673c48431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d07801cb571591a08354a4a95f9d9eaf5f61bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=4\\sqrt{5}-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}} \\Longrightarrow \\frac{12}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"208\" height=\"43\" /> so the requested ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8dea4894dc4221a8a4026e9fbb875f64ed5dd758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8:12=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 2:3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"149\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Magnetoninja\">Magnetoninja</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/_0YaCyxiMBo\">https://youtu.be/_0YaCyxiMBo</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=4245\">https://youtu.be/4_x1sgcQCp4?t=4245</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2>